        "original_id": "b0e4dde0-3b6b-5782-96a1-8df237219edd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Frankenheimer, Tiffanie DeBartolo, Jennifer Aniston, Burt Lancaster, Edward Anhalt, Evan Hunter\n- Works: Dream for an Insomniac, The Young Savages\n- Roles: film director, television director, writer\n- Topics: American film, television, crime drama\n\nFacts:\n- John Frankenheimer was born on February 19, 1930, and he was an American film and television director known for social dramas and action/suspense films.\n- The Young Savages is a 1961 crime drama film directed by John Frankenheimer, starring Burt Lancaster, and written by Edward Anhalt from a novel by Evan Hunter.\n- In 1996, Tiffanie DeBartolo wrote and directed Dream for an Insomniac, a film featuring Jennifer Aniston that had a very limited release.\n- John Frankenheimer died on July 6, 2002.",
